   "notes": "28 Petty Cury, north side, Boots 'CHEMISTS' range: 1920s-30s neo-Tudor ashlar with three steep coped gables with finials. Ground floor: open colonnade of four square stone piers carrying a carved entablature (lettered CHEMISTS, heraldic shields) at ~4.5 m, dark-blue Boots shopfronts set back behind (piers not modelled as pilasters since they stop at the entablature). First floor: one wide stone-mullioned and transomed leaded window per bay; one 2-light mullioned window in each gable. Bay centres assumed regular (3 x 4.9 m); gable tops above the DSM eave are not representable."
